/* ==========================================================================
   shellref — command data
   ==========================================================================
   This is the ONLY file you should need to touch to add, edit, or remove a
   command. Everything else (rendering, search, the sidebar, the generator)
   reads from the DATA array below — nothing else needs to change.

   To add a new command, copy an existing object and adjust the fields:

     {
       s:    'files',                 // section key — must match a key in
                                       // js/sections.js -> SECTION_META
       t:    'Everyday file ops',     // tier/subheading shown above the card
       sh:   'powershell',            // OPTIONAL shell badge: 'cmd' | 'powershell' | 'unix'
                                       // (omit for commands that only exist in one
                                       // shell context, e.g. Git or Docker commands)
       cmd:  'Copy-Item a b -Recurse',// the command shown as the card title
       desc: 'What it does, briefly.',
       use:  'OPTIONAL — when you would actually reach for this.',
       ex:   'Copy-Item C:\\a C:\\b -Recurse', // example invocation shown in the copy box
       kw:   'copy files recursive'   // OPTIONAL extra search keywords not
                                       // already covered by cmd/desc/ex
     },

   To add a brand-new SECTION (category), you only need to touch two places:
     1. Add an entry for it to SECTION_META in js/sections.js
     2. Tag any DATA items below with that section's key (the `s` field)
   The sidebar, "All commands" view (if you list it there), and the Command
   Generator's category list all pick it up automatically — no HTML edits.
   ========================================================================== */

